      <slug></slug>
      <title>ZFS in Open Source Operating Systems</title>
      <subtitle>zfs</subtitle>
      <track>BSD devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract></abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The Zettabyte Filesystem (ZFS) is one of the most advanced open-source&#xA;filesystems available today. It comes from (Open-)Solaris and ships with&#xA;the FreeBSD operating system. This talk will give a short introduction&#xA;to ZFS, list supported operating systems, briefly explain legal and license&#xA;issues and give a look at its (possible) future.&lt;/p&gt;      </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="3351">Martin Matuska</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>